lessons.body:
A stressed final -ah usually marks a feminine singular noun or adjective: {0}
"year", {1} "for a wife".

-ayim marks a pair, or "two of": {2} "two days", {3}
"hands". Body parts that come in pairs use it: hands, eyes, feet, ears.

An unstressed -ah is a different ending, "toward" (L2.8). The transliteration's stress mark
tells them apart.
